#!/usr/bin/env sh
# Surakkha pre-commit hook (managed by husky).
# Runs ESLint (--max-warnings 0) + prose-lint on staged source files only.
#
# Two checks, both run via `lint-staged`:
#   - ESLint for structural issues (TS rules + React + a11y + import)
#   - prose-lint for AI-slop signatures (hedge words, all-caps shouting)
#
# Per CONTRIBUTING.md, "pnpm lint must pass locally" is a merge-blocker.
# This hook runs only against files in the user's current diff, so:
#   - a warning on a staged file blocks the commit;
#   - pre-existing lint debt in unrelated files does not.
#
# Bypass with `git commit --no-verify` for documented escape-hatch cases.
# When bypassing, note the reason in the PR body so reviewers can audit.
pnpm lint:staged
